text.section:
The full Board, by majority vote, shall have the power to suspend, revoke, or refuse to renew the license of any professional geologist who, after an appropriate formal hearing, is found to have been involved in:

Any fraud or deceit in obtaining licensure;


Any violation of the Code of Professional Ethics and Conduct or other regulations of the Board;


Demonstrated gross negligence, incompetence, or misconduct in the practice of geology as a professional geologist; or


Any conviction of a felony which, in the opinion of the Board, would adversely affect the practice of geology.
